            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Victoria Ford Everett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What I changed:\nI cooked the apples for far longer than the recipe called for because my family prefers less crunchy apples in their cobbler. \n\nI added more buttermilk and oil to the topping mix to make it more creamy and easier to spread over the cobbler. These extra additions keep the topping from looking undercooked and lumpy.\n\nMade this awesome dish for my neighbor who lost her husband, and then for my mother-in-law and father-in-law. They all loved it! Biggest compliment was that they couldn't tell I had made them something sugar-free and more healthy. I will def. be making this again for my family get togethers and as presents for diabetic friends.",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-07T04:39:42.730Z"
          },
